WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Speaker 1: Welcome back to the David Pakman&nbsp;
show. I am Farron Cousins from Ring of Fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.600
sitting in for David Pakman. I've been sitting in&nbsp;
for David all of this week. He will return to you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:16.880
on Monday. I promise he has given me his word,&nbsp;
but. Let's finish things up here, shall we?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.760
And of course, as I've done every day this week,&nbsp;
you got to talk a little bit about Joe Manchin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:30.720
Public Enemy number one. And now we're finding&nbsp;
out that Republicans, including Senate Minority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.160
Leader Mitch McConnell, are actively trying&nbsp;
to recruit Joe Manchin over to the dark side.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:43.040
Come to us officially. They're telling him. And&nbsp;
that's not hyperbole, either, literally. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:49.680
been reported that John Cornyn admitted to sending&nbsp;
Joe Manchin a text message, inviting him to come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.560
and join the Republican Party in the Senate.&nbsp;
Where are your friends? You're just like us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:01.840
Come on, Joe. What do you say? Mitch McConnell,&nbsp;
however, said in an interview with The New York&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:08.400
Times. Obviously, we would love to have him on our&nbsp;
team. I think he'd be more comfortable. Why in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:14.400
world would they? The Democrats want to call him&nbsp;
a liar and try to hotbox him and embarrass him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.680
I think the message is we don't want you&nbsp;
around. Obviously, that is up to Joe Manchin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:29.200
but he is clearly not welcome on that side of&nbsp;
the aisle. Joe Manchin himself this week also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.440
talked about the the bullying that he is&nbsp;
receiving from those on the left for killing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.840
the build back better act and said, you know,&nbsp;
they ought to push me into the Republican Party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.400
That's what he said. And I think these Republicans&nbsp;
took that as if they're not going to push you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:54.240
We're going to try to pull you. So come on,&nbsp;
Joe. And to be honest, think about it this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.400
way. Obviously, if Joe Manchin were to leave the&nbsp;
Democratic Party, go over to the Republicans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:02.320
they get the majority, they take over the&nbsp;
committees and all of that. It's horrible, right?&nbsp;

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:08.720
Unidentified: Right. Is it?
Speaker 1: The Democrats are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:14.960
already struggling to get anything done because&nbsp;
they have only 50 and Republicans have 50.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.920
And Joe Manchin is the biggest&nbsp;
roadblock now I understand 100&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.160
percent if Joe Manchin were to leave, the&nbsp;
Democrats become a Republican, give them the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:33.840
majority. Nothing gets done. You know, the Voting&nbsp;
Rights Act? Kiss that goodbye. Any chance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:40.160
getting a different version of build back better&nbsp;
gone. But what are the chances of those things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:46.640
happening with Joe Manchin as a Democrat anyway?&nbsp;
Wouldn't it make more sense electorally speaking?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.560
For the Democrats to boot, Joe Manchin, don't&nbsp;
give him the option. Tell him you're out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:01.520
And then let the Republicans take the fall for&nbsp;
it. The public wants the build back better act.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.080
So if you can pin the whole thing on Republicans,&nbsp;
if Joe Manchin were to go over there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.040
Wouldn't that be a better campaign message? You&nbsp;
know, look, we tried to give you all these things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:20.240
and it got so bad that one of our guys ended up&nbsp;
becoming a Republican because he hates it so much.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:27.200
He doesn't want you to have good things. So he's&nbsp;
joining the party that continuously refuses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.160
let you have good things because that's what&nbsp;
they stand for, because that's who they are.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.760
So if you want these things, we&nbsp;
got to get the majority back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.160
Now, as again, I've talked about that this&nbsp;
week, Republicans have to defend 20 seats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:53.920
20 seats in 20, 22. That requires a lot of&nbsp;
money. And the odds significantly reduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:57.840
that you're going to hold on to every single&nbsp;
one of those seats, the more you have to defend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.920
You also have members who are considering&nbsp;
retirement, some who've already announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.880
retirement. So in those new races, of course,&nbsp;
that's going to be far more expensive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:14.080
and it opens the door for a Democrat&nbsp;
challenger to seize the seat. So.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.880
Democrats could probably come&nbsp;
up with a winning message&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:27.840
by getting rid of Joe Manchin because again, then&nbsp;
the entire boogeyman becomes the Republican Party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:35.120
I'm just throwing it out there as a possibility,&nbsp;
as a very real electoral strategy that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:40.720
Democratic Party should at least consider. And&nbsp;
if you're not willing to kick Joe Manchin out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.280
we're not willing to push him over to the&nbsp;
other side. Then at the very least, don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:51.280
let him get his hands on the DNC money when he's&nbsp;
not going to support the Democratic Party itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.560
I mean, after all, reports have also come out&nbsp;
this week saying that he is receiving so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:02.080
corporate cash right before he announced that&nbsp;
he was not going to be supporting the build back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.640
better act. So Joe Manchin will be fine. Hell,&nbsp;
he's not even up for reelection for a while.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:15.840
So don't worry about him. Kick him out. Make him&nbsp;
part of the enemy. And see what you can come up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:22.880
with in terms of electoral strategy messaging,&nbsp;
once that happens. You keep them in the party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.080
You're going to have to deal with him and his&nbsp;
problems and the negativity that he brings with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:35.040
him for at least another full year. And to me&nbsp;
personally, I just don't think that's worth it.

